<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Precisely 13,266 games have been played si=
nce the inception of the Premier League, and 19 of those matches have finis=
hed 4-4 (0.1%), a rarity in a division dominated by the mighty 1-0 (17.6%).=
 It was about time we got one, though. The months of August and September, =
when teams are still fighting to define their top-flight seasons and fitnes=
s and motivation tend to be at their peak, have never seen a single 4-4 dra=
w. As motivation decreases the chances of stupid scorelines increase, and t=
hat=E2=80=99s where the 4-4 creeps in. There=E2=80=99s a certain on-the-bea=
chness inherent in the score, and it is no coincidence that it has occurred=
 more in the second half of April, as thoughts drift to the close season an=
d the ineffable pointlessness of a lot of late-campaign football becomes un=
avoidable, than in the entirety of any other month.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Though scoring four goals in a single game=
 is quite encouraging, conceding four in the same one is suggestive of poor=
 planning. Of the 22 clubs to have been involved in a Premier League 4-4, h=
alf are no longer in the Premier League at all. Only Manchester City in 202=
3-24 have <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_=
JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDdU1IxeDnOTgt6YHM8QyEWI-d8NQM6CQLdFB=
yBnVKMQGLppQxI8jd5n_DTkv8YW_dXSY6uW3-2LmBe5LDiUpXEy8KMxy3okuXVkkKbLhNSNAbyK=
hWtB6Mwv1gR45QOuy_7igEu8PtDDGkrEOJJj3VmWpAEayrQJBFhPzwa6ZAWp1ZDKjjTdJzKJKDv=
ySR_qxwLnYxYNT9lirLhWJe36dV1zkAmbqcXbgR2Aoe5ikQEOMeh9wlbGhPFmR1tUGZ62Tw/4vl=
/KJNslp0qRw6wTY-1vD10Qw/h28/h001.UrNC5JZXHt8ZHbrOVuMci_h2eBIL2s0khNKBR9k5dT=
c" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">played out a 4-4 draw</a> and won the league i=
n the same season, while six teams have recorded the scoreline and promptly=
 gone down. It is an inherently unserious score, which duly attracts unseri=
ous teams. Manchester United, being as they were a very serious team for a =
long while after its creation, had won the Premier League 11 times before t=
hey were involved in one. When they <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDRQ3pEajJq=
G1YLACUWWSCCJozHPOkdXfCwzXQlAvik1vQZkqyurr9d9uNxbI1Vf3TlukDUDHWyC2nzakd_O9K=
Cj-_6vxcVadsr7EPdjaF7aa_fVeOQwbF_hPU9o7uq60J6lPKSFtZ9aDzJO83R5E4bdi1EgBdLbA=
YkbGSPNIAPY5NyqrCWabHBacDNdB4l7V1211B8D6NmrLI-nCP3asAMOYCm65IlRtHeN5GfC8LOU=
Fw9tkniMT65bfC7xcIs57k/4vl/KJNslp0qRw6wTY-1vD10Qw/h29/h001.LJksB2Bw8SwolkeE=
WsofqqlxTrRm2RTOYqwychxykJY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">drew 4-4 with Everto=
n</a> in late April (obviously) 2012 it was their first 4-4 draw since 1974=
. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFu=
ifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgypssBVgrWCCDuCL2s-v3E4=
ERToLNW_J59CZJqQXfkyO0rMDdaQRlCVrHPp70Jbd_ys-dwNV2KTDlU6FUt0WaKKcu9u8SFsLnd=
N_m7_2p9HY-2eiMpkqpUGbteJMPt_b3Gd3N4MMOVdgMKJPCK4O2NyN09jzolp658I9UoHR0hNTl=
qQqgaJqtABjT7cNYBeVa5xTvVK8w77itpaLSCBsoFHh3iL-nOK524sbOSe8v-GWUbm1YLWKl5PZ=
Mr4EiNS-Z/4vl/KJNslp0qRw6wTY-1vD10Qw/h30/h001.id3rFVz3ki1B691-Nc4j_j7_zyBQq=
tBv0kUI2zW0jKM" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Sunday=E2=80=99s against Aston Vi=
lla</a> was their second in a year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The effect is obviously quite discombobula=
ting. Fans at Old Trafford on Sunday, as United fell two goals down, recove=
red, fell two goals down again and recovered again, didn=E2=80=99t know whe=
ther to laugh, cry, boo, cheer, leave early or stay late and most chose a c=
ombination. =E2=80=9CI thought we were by far the better team,=E2=80=9D <a =
href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_X=
G18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgxhvmoPyx6WSj2H6yLo5StGVfFVs=
Qy72311eJUxMxSeomeJJMYPvER27sHVvCyyfcBWBLrxCv4HxbORW-3TjmNdSnh0bkmARGTH1cX_=
MrEKKHF4-XICxKYOzFQOlFwYIS5efEAppetcmphmY1fbiAIPzK1wMXQtlWG4DOT9GlUQK-Dkrkl=
y_-ZLYUV_FoMwPTiMcjqmMhzIsxGXAGcOXfQ53skvgwS9b91r_A4FOyel1w3It-yzLSnZukxaHR=
gW1J60uRvb2mt9Em48T-azcRMQ/4vl/KJNslp0qRw6wTY-1vD10Qw/h31/h001.2a8p6fWl8uw3=
S7UFs0XtNzoElgrsKpzso9o1lSUT7tY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">cooed Michael Ca=
rrick</a>, the obviously nice guy currently being forced to find awkward wa=
ys of looking on the bright side in <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYc=
aNsDra0BxnPgN62JDv85oXTF5vHXJ1zPeQMLE8mONcCWuqxMV3L1ajyUHaQcmXzW1N6LgQIezyZ=
jRcFb2IN7kw-sfqrKvGuU4kFR6IoXazC8EV6OtFpKbccFf3D6XsaLBcpsy3F7QI1UyQofv1T45d=
nd19fiG89eWzTfsPHGT_GiaUuwAOK4XPsMh0Pv8DNByUyqxvEA7SO1ZpQBtLFzKzc0eqEubmJwp=
Rmpg0OP5fECG9ButlwhS2dngrHby7NH6tqf3Eq9LFux/4vl/KJNslp0qRw6wTY-1vD10Qw/h32/=
h001.zIyIKGtucsrI-EJ5fKEzB3CvEuIfqsaVXsJpJO8tLkY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;"=
>generally miserable post-match interviews</a>. =E2=80=9CThey started, scor=
ed, then we played some very, very good football. We were the better team f=
or large parts of the game. We=E2=80=99re making it difficult for ourselves=
 with the goals we=E2=80=99re giving away.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">He may be on to something there. United ha=
ve now conceded first in 80% of their home games this season, a figure only=
 Crystal Palace, also the only team with fewer points than them, can match,=
 and his team=E2=80=99s chances of success would probably improve if they s=
topped doing it. And then there=E2=80=99s Villa, new masters of this silly =
scoreline, the club who in 1995 were involved in the Premier League=E2=80=
=99s first ever 4-4 draw and have now also played in the most recent, in th=
e process moving joint top of the all-time 4-4 charts. Inevitably the teams=
 most likely to have secured many of these have tended to be both rubbish e=
nough to go around drawing 4-4 and also not quite rubbish enough to also ge=
t relegated, bad enough to concede loads of goals yet also good enough to s=
core quite a few. This does feel like prime Everton territory but it is Tot=
tenham =E2=80=93 who lead the all-time Premier League goal concession ranki=
ngs =E2=80=93 and Villa =E2=80=93 still the only team to draw 4-4 twice in =
the same season, back in 2007-08 =E2=80=93 who have more than anyone else. =
Their running tally of 4-4 draws? Why, 4-4, obviously.</p>
